  "decision": "FAIL / NO_CANDIDATE_ADMITTED / NO_ROBUST_FACTOR_PASS. F-CBOE-PC-EXECUTION preserved frozen V11-like drawdown but did not add incremental execution alpha. On the preregistered 2013+ window candidate CAGR 12.603870% was below V11 12.639383%, candidate Sharpe 1.449526 was slightly below V11 1.450450 and below the availability-matched unconditional one-session delay control 1.453601, and the candidate beat the matched control in only 4/7 fixed folds. The matched control itself was also below V11 in 2013+ CAGR, so a one-session U.S.-increase delay is not a new return source. Paired 63-session moving-block bootstrap over 20,000 replicates gave P(CAGR candidate > V11)=20.245% and P(Sharpe candidate > matched)=31.320%; both median incremental deltas were negative. Candidate bootstrap MDD P97.5 was 12.559%, and cumulative 34-trial DSR probability was 95.552%, but DSR alone cannot override the failed incremental gates. Per the frozen stop rule, no threshold, sign, smoothing, delay-length, start-date, asset-scope, or execution-rule rescue is permitted. The Cboe Equity Put/Call signal is rejected for this retrospective V11 execution-timing use.",
